  "summary": "Both failures had the same root cause on this side: the `fileUrl` we returned was not something a browser could actually fetch.\n\n**Tracker export (empty screen)** — `POST /api/v1/tracker/export` returned a *relative* path (`/api/v1/tracker/exports/{id}`). Opened in a new tab it resolves against the SPA origin, which serves the app shell — a blank screen. It now returns an absolute URL on this API (`settings.api_base_url`, from `API_BASE_URL`).\n\n**Contract download** — `GET /api/v1/contracts/{contractId}/document/download` returned `doc.storage_path` (`/documents/<id>/v1.pdf`), a bookkeeping string with no route and no bytes behind it. Now:\n- Uploaded third-party-paper bytes are actually persisted (`app/services/files.py` → `settings.document_storage_dir`), and generated Version 1 documents are written as real files (PDF through the same hand-rolled writer the exports use; merged body as text otherwise) in `app/services/contract_documents.py`.\n- New `GET /api/v1/contracts/{contractId}/document/file` serves those raw bytes with `Content-Disposition: attachment; filename=\"…\"`.\n- `download` now returns an absolute URL to that route, or the existing AF-005 retrieval error when no bytes exist.\n\n**Auth for the second fetch** — the browser follows a `fileUrl` directly and cannot attach `Authorization`, so both byte endpoints accept either the bearer token or a short-lived, path-bound signed `token` carried in the URL (`create_file_token`/`decode_file_token`, `file_access_user`/`file_access_tenant_id`). Never a public link: a token for one file is rejected on another, and role checks still apply. `POST /auth/refresh` already exists and is unchanged.\n\nChecks: `python -m compileall app` clean, `pytest -q` → 528 passed (added round-trip and token-replay tests; updated the two export tests that asserted the old relative URL). Reading taken: fix the two broken flows only — no changes to tab DTOs or other endpoints. The frontend side (fetching `fileUrl` with credentials rather than a bare `window.open`, if it wants the bearer path) belongs to the other repository.",
