    "notes": "Auth is now Authorization: Bearer (JWT) plus the refresh cookie; the X-User-Role/X-User-Id stub is gone. The refresh route is mounted at BOTH /api/v1/auth/refresh and /auth/refresh (app.main includes the auth router twice, with and without the /api/v1 prefix), so the counterpart's POST /auth/refresh works. fileUrl from both download endpoints is an absolute URL (settings.api_base_url + path) pointing at GET /api/v1/contracts/{contractId}/document/file or GET /api/v1/tracker/exports/{fileId}; each carries a signed short-lived ?token= query param pinned to that exact path, so it works with or without an Authorization header, and both return raw bytes with Content-Disposition. tab accepts exactly Ownership, CycleTime, Bottleneck, Turnaround and format exactly Excel, PDF. dateRangeFrom/dateRangeTo are validated date strings (typed as string on the wire, not a date type)."
